  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "/yx1dZXMp8s+86VmMl4KXsJimS4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:08.642Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The shipped defaults are `EXECUTIONS_DATA_PRUNE=true`, `EXECUTIONS_DATA_MAX_AGE=336` hours and `EXECUTIONS_DATA_PRUNE_MAX_COUNT=10000`. The documentation confirms the behaviour rather than merely permitting it: *\"n8n enables pruning by default\"*, removing *\"finished executions along with their execution data and binary data\"* when either the age or the count threshold trips.\n\nBeing fair to n8n, it does save successful runs \u2014 `EXECUTIONS_DATA_SAVE_ON_SUCCESS` defaults to `all`. The gap is not that it never records. It is that it records and then deletes on a timer, 336 hours being fourteen days.\n\nThat is a defensible design for an orchestrator whose execution log is a debugging aid. It is disqualifying for anything expected to answer a question a year later.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:08.642804Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:08.642808Z"
    }
  },
